    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "addrman: use uniform sampling inside buckets",
    "user": {
      "login": "sipa",
      "id": 548488,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjU0ODQ4OA==",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/548488?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/sipa",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sipa",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sipa/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sipa/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sipa/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sipa/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sipa/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sipa/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sipa/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sipa/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sipa/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "The current way we sample from addresses within a bucket in addrman is randomized, but not perfectly random. It uses a linear scan, starting at a random position (out of the 64 positions in a bucket). This means that if for example only position 17 and 20 contain an address, 17 will be picked with probability 95.3% (whenever the initial position is 21..63 or 0..17) and 20 will be picked with probability 4.7% (whenever the initial position is 18..20).\r\n\r\nMake this search perfectly uniform, regardless of distribution of addresses within the bucket, by first copying all non-empty positions to a temporary array, and then selecting uniformly randomly from that array.\r\n\r\nSuggested by Crypt-iQ.",
